fbe7a8eedbebbdf169140a4b45f9e86004828aeeac5a8ba99d95" :answer-field/choices ["q-109731/selection/fd002462a5cbbc28e67e51b07de4cbdf8bf58a6763a40075ec4c82f73a1ec7a4" "q-109731/selection/d2939398742d130980158a80319f37e64fa09d599243a1dcc585e7ae719b25f8" "q-109731/selection/f16fdb0c3d7ffbe7a8eedbebbdf169140a4b45f9e86004828aeeac5a8ba99d95" "q-109731/selection/7743200bbdb3418f78720aa2c9f6d4e790e6f343a46375b147d85fcf8f9dd78e" "q-109731/selection/3fbc09c24819a466ee71b51721ead3a2164e4cd14fd0b4c436b4902b29dbf341"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109731" :question/id #uuid "0ac435d5-873e-5e20-9afd-d167334f9b60" :question/math-academy-id "q-109731" :question/problem "The vector-valued function $r(x,\\theta )$ parametrizes the surface of revolution generated by rotating the curve $y=1+\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ by $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis for $x\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{3\\pi }{4}].$ Which of the following could be $r?$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071875/assets/56a380b075d10862170ed9c9a45c07dddff3eaef1ea9fb3109a61cc3d27b5ac4.png)\n\n \n\nA point $(x,y,z)$ on the surface generated by rotating the graph of $y=f(x)$ by $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis for $x\\in [a,b]$ has the position vector\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=⟨x,\\,f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩,\\,x\\in [a,b],\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that $y=f(x)=1+\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{3\\pi }{4}].$\n\nSo, the parametrization of our surface of revolution is \n\n$$\nr(x,\\theta )=⟨x,\\,(1+\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,(1+\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩,\\,x\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{3\\pi }{4}],\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109731/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ac4af78-af9b-5d48-a5d7-7d47ad92e348"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109731"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109718/selection/d8c1f445310c443e90e1ee4af90ecc5880635f3f7a3d3bc21ca08fa1b491e6a8" :answer/id #uuid "986271dd-3153-5038-a58d-1697523056bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{x}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109718/selection/2adf321adfaadcbb152345e687f46a43926d9e1c985d70c736ab18c87fba3ce9" :answer/id #uuid "74b50d89-d0f6-5689-bf70-b769dc21f3f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109718/selection/3c3c656552e91080115d65b3482d8efdd4b141d7b8a2bfb13981bed1aae4d073" :answer/id #uuid "795ae949-b89f-56fe-84ca-d7cc5a303cac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{x}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109718/selection/38b66f874ad41b2fb0761c6338192c2ee6d31035e2466b71cbc78aad3cbab216" :answer/id #uuid "90e4b619-bbc9-58da-ba47-c0bb4a3580e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109718/selection/5bfc31cb0f00459e667c094ebc911385abc3af185b17634b92a03c09da8da04d" :answer/id #uuid "ba638e4c-084b-5ed3-ae04-d9adfc24012b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109718/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "16c56699-6d0e-5eef-b9c7-5d6e8126124b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109718/selection/5bfc31cb0f00459e667c094ebc911385abc3af185b17634b92a03c09da8da04d" :answer-field/choices ["q-109718/selection/d8c1f445310c443e90e1ee4af90ecc5880635f3f7a3d3bc21ca08fa1b491e6a8" "q-109718/selection/2adf321adfaadcbb152345e687f46a43926d9e1c985d70c736ab18c87fba3ce9" "q-109718/selection/3c3c656552e91080115d65b3482d8efdd4b141d7b8a2bfb13981bed1aae4d073" "q-109718/selection/38b66f874ad41b2fb0761c6338192c2ee6d31035e2466b71cbc78aad3cbab216" "q-109718/selection/5bfc31cb0f00459e667c094ebc911385abc3af185b17634b92a03c09da8da04d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109718" :question/id #uuid "57494b1e-2aae-569c-8de2-ca632c8af9a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-109718" :question/problem "$$\nr(x,\\theta )=⟨x,\\,\\text{_______},\\,\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $r(x,\\theta )$ above parametrizes the surface of revolution generated by rotating the curve $y=\\sqrt{x}$ by $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis for $x\\in [0,4].$ What is the second component of $r?$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071875/assets/56a380b075d10862170ed9c9a45c07dddff3eaef1ea9fb3109a61cc3d27b5ac4.png)\n\n  \n\nA point $(x,y,z)$ on the surface generated by rotating the graph of $y=f(x)$ by $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis for $x\\in [a,b]$ has the position vector\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=⟨x,\\,f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩,\\,x\\in [a,b],\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that $y=f(x)=\\sqrt{x}\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in [0,4].$ \n\nSo, the parametrization of our surface of revolution is\n\n$$\nr(x,\\theta )=⟨x,\\,\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩,\\,x\\in [0,4],\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, the second component of $r$ is $\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-109718/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ac4af78-af9b-5d48-a5d7-7d47ad92e348"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109718"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-157493/selection/fedfccee8fda928440d7fd7f9e6cc41e9c46669c4ce66bb8cb48d40bc52bc100" :answer/id #uuid "e9cd4cb4