^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109721/selection/bfdf353da865a45d9c1291c3a657b0f329c3f1b4cffb37aafbfb7bc36b0b7931" :answer/id #uuid "74e8c101-de51-514a-af90-8f3dfcc5ee2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi {x}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109721/selection/89a5d52cfe4970cd1cad13e8df6223bb9c2cb8be3185dcaee462751198b266ca" :answer/id #uuid "dc975fa0-3c47-5667-b128-9e245dbc23b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi (4{x}^{2}-{x}^{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109721/selection/2ee2a3a559d61f5d4e1d2940c8dbfc8d142b7d138eab427ba0ddd5ff28f4e405" :answer/id #uuid "e2a7aa63-8ea7-5b4a-b540-8010c76d7b5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2x-{x}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109721/selection/8f1ebe48539e88148e9ee0eb53a784a303f1072ce340cd41f9480acf1f1b432d" :answer/id #uuid "845d8f2d-8ad2-51ab-b1af-068efd143b80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(4{x}^{2}-{x}^{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109721/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "eb97e2b6-5623-5d52-bed0-c5fe57d8882f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109721/selection/8f1ebe48539e88148e9ee0eb53a784a303f1072ce340cd41f9480acf1f1b432d" :answer-field/choices ["q-109721/selection/00d566890ec9289188bfc0081eee7ced53ecf886e13068ff413fe4ebbc744ac2" "q-109721/selection/bfdf353da865a45d9c1291c3a657b0f329c3f1b4cffb37aafbfb7bc36b0b7931" "q-109721/selection/89a5d52cfe4970cd1cad13e8df6223bb9c2cb8be3185dcaee462751198b266ca" "q-109721/selection/2ee2a3a559d61f5d4e1d2940c8dbfc8d142b7d138eab427ba0ddd5ff28f4e405" "q-109721/selection/8f1ebe48539e88148e9ee0eb53a784a303f1072ce340cd41f9480acf1f1b432d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109721" :question/id #uuid "5fa86f80-b55e-5f6e-9513-d6dfc2c505bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-109721" :question/problem "$$\nr(x,\\theta )=⟨x,\\,\\text{_______},\\,(4{x}^{2}-{x}^{4})\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $r(x,\\theta )$ above parametrizes the surface of revolution generated by rotating the curve $y=4{x}^{2}-{x}^{4}$ by $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis for $x\\in [-2,2].$ What is the second component of $r?$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071875/assets/56a380b075d10862170ed9c9a45c07dddff3eaef1ea9fb3109a61cc3d27b5ac4.png)\n\n \n\nA point $(x,y,z)$ on the surface generated by rotating the graph of $y=f(x)$ by $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis for $x\\in [a,b]$ has the position vector\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=⟨x,\\,f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩,\\,x\\in [a,b],\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that $y=f(x)=4{x}^{2}-{x}^{4}\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in [-2,2].$ \n\nSo, the parametrization of our surface of revolution is\n\n$$\nr(x,\\theta )=⟨x,\\,(4{x}^{2}-{x}^{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,(4{x}^{2}-{x}^{4})\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩,\\,x\\in [-2,2],\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, the second component of $r$ is $(4{x}^{2}-{x}^{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-109721/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ac4af78-af9b-5d48-a5d7-7d47ad92e348"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109721"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109734/selection/fb1c829ce88da7f16807d2507c0babfd248aa897e991a7ea7d750bfaf760c3bc" :answer/id #uuid "2604c29b-0f41-5ead-ab19-fbf0ec2f4596" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,x⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109734/selection