s/04de4ea7dc617be1429c596812ce4f450c2cdaafd8d94d86f75e68a6743acba9.png)\n\nA point $(x,y,z)$ on the surface generated by rotating the graph of $y=f(z)$ by $2\\pi $ radians about the $z$-axis has the position vector \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=⟨f(z)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,f(z)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,z⟩,\\,z\\in [a,b],\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that $y=f(z)={2}^{z}-1\\ge 0$ for all $z\\in [0,2].$\n\nSo, the parametrization of our surface of revolution is\n\n$$\nr(z,\\theta )=⟨({2}^{z}-1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,({2}^{z}-1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,z⟩,\\,z\\in [0,2],\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the first component of $r$ is $({2}^{z}-1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-161036/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b85acdfc-0505-5472-b5f3-53270bffa030"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161036"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-156978/selection/134cf868619d383af1b1b7817c3dca4e75d549692ac1b0186c76b50cff0e709d" :answer/id #uuid "845b15eb-2bc0-539a-9917-488186c9454a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨y,\\,{sin}^{2}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,{cos}^{2}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-156978/selection/842c4a123a77fe1143703edf05b496fbf437313967616a84c7b2807d05429d8b" :answer/id #uuid "ce8ab582-403e-5368-8b85-66c85bf30328" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨{sin}^{2}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y,\\,{sin}^{2}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-156978/selection/e77cab7286d7262138ebbaf5253c93e3909bbfdaf2d500e04fce4c4ba063cb3f" :answer/id #uuid "8ea3f16d-5e1b-5713-9fe3-10f3e2e78702" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨y,\\,{sin}^{2}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,{sin}^{2}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-